# Alfajores Argentinean Style

Based on [https://www.allrecipes.com/recipe/187786/alfajores-argentinean-style/](https://www.allrecipes.com/recipe/187786/alfajores-argentinean-style) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20250505122019/https://www.allrecipes.com/recipe/187786/alfajores-argentinean-style/))

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### Cookies

- [ ] 2 ½ cups [cornstarch]{ ing="cornstarch" }
- [ ] 1 ⅔ cups [unbleached all-purpose flour]{ ing="unbleached-all-purpose-flour" }
- [ ] 2 teaspoons [baking powder]{ ing="baking-powder" }
- [ ] ½ teaspoon [baking soda]{ ing="baking-soda" }
- [ ] 1 cup [unsalted butter]{ ing="unsalted-butter" }, softened
- [ ] ¾ cup [white sugar]{ ing="white-sugar" }
- [ ] 3 [egg yolks]{ ing="egg-yolks" }
- [ ] 2 teaspoons [lemon zest]{ ing="lemon-zest" }
- [ ] 1 teaspoon [vanilla rum]{ ing="vanilla-rum" }
- [ ] ½ teaspoon [vanilla extract]{ ing="vanilla-extract" }
- [ ] ½ teaspoon [lemon extract]{ ing="lemon-extract" }

### Filling

- [ ] 1 (11.5 ounce) jar [dulce de leche]{ ing="dulce-de-leche" }
- [ ] ½ cup [unsweetened shredded coconut]{ ing="unsweetened-shredded-coconut" }

## Recipe

1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). Line baking sheets with parchment paper.
1. Whisk [cornstarch]{ ing="cornstarch" }, [flour]{ ing="unbleached-all-purpose-flour" }, [baking powder]{ ing="baking-powder" }, and [baking soda]{ ing="baking-soda" } together; set aside.
1. Beat [butter]{ ing="unsalted-butter" } and [sugar]{ ing="white-sugar" } together in a large bowl with an electric mixer until light and fluffy. Beat in 2 [egg yolks]{ ing="egg-yolks" }, one at a time, beating well after each addition; beat in third yolk along with [lemon zest]{ ing="lemon-zest" }, [vanilla rum]{ ing="vanilla-rum" }, [vanilla extract]{ ing="vanilla-extract" }, and [lemon extract]{ ing="lemon-extract" }. Gently fold in cornstarch mixture with a spoon, making a crumbly dough, until cohesive enough; press into a ball. Wrap dough in plastic wrap; chill 30 to 60 minutes.
1. Roll dough out, using as little flour as possible, until about ¼-inch thick. (The dough will have an unusual consistency.) Cut dough using a small round cookie cutter. Continue pressing dough together, rolling, and cutting until all dough is used. Place cookies spaced ½-inch apart onto the prepared cookie sheets.
1. Bake in the preheated oven until set but not browned, 7 to 10 minutes. Transfer cookies immediately to a wire rack to cool.
1. Spread 1 teaspoon [dulce de leche]{ ing="dulce-de-leche" } onto underside of 1 cooled cookie; sandwich with second cookie until caramel oozes out sides. Roll sides in [shredded coconut]{ ing="unsweetened-shredded-coconut" }. Repeat with remaining cookies, dulce de leche, and coconut.

## Notes

- Alfajores are Argentina’s most popular cookies—delicate, melt-in-your-mouth sandwich cookies made with cornstarch-based shortbread filled with dulce de leche (caramel-like spread)
- Commonly enjoyed at breakfast with coffee or tea, as an afternoon snack, or for special gatherings
- Variations include dusting with powdered sugar, coating with chocolate, or rolling in almonds instead of coconut
